jags
------------------------------------------
JAGS is Just Another Gibbs Sampler. It is a program for analysis of Bayesian
hierarchical models using Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) simulation not
wholly unlike BUGS.

Runtime requirements:
  bash-5.2.21-1
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  libjags-devel-5.0.0-1bl1
  libjags5-5.0.0-1bl1
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  libltdl7-2.6.2-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.8-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cppunit-1.13.2-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://mcmc-jags.sourceforge.io/

Canonical download:
  mirror://sourceforge/mcmc-jags/JAGS-5.0.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack jags-5.0.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./jags-5.0.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/jags-5.0.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/jags-5.0.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libjags5-5.0.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libjags-devel-5.0.0-X.tar.xz

